---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="How we research and write | Medical Rank" description="How Medical Rank researches, sources, writes and corrects its guides and articles.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="pagehead">
      <h1>How we research and write</h1>
      <p class="lede">What you can expect from a page on Medical Rank, and how to tell us when we get something wrong.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Guides</h2>
      <p>Guides are written and checked by hand. Each one lists the documents it relies on, usually the platform's own documentation, with the date we last checked them. Where a guide rests on our own experience or judgment and not on a document, it says so. Where we could not confirm something, the guide has a section called "How we checked this" that states the limit.</p>
      <h2>Articles</h2>
      <p>Articles are produced differently. Topics are chosen from what practices search for. Drafts are written with AI assistance from that research, checked by automated rules for structure and unsupported claims, and published on a schedule. They are not individually reviewed by a person before publication. We read them afterwards and correct or remove any that fall short. If an article and a guide disagree, trust the guide.</p>
      <h2>What we will not publish</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Rankings or results promises.</li>
        <li>Testimonials, client figures or case studies without permission and evidence.</li>
        <li>Pages generated by swapping a city or specialty name into a template.</li>
        <li>Medical, legal or compliance advice. We describe marketing practice; check legal questions with your own counsel.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Commercial interest</h2>
      <p>Medical Rank sells marketing services to practices. That interest is disclosed on the pages where it is relevant and does not decide what a guide concludes.</p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>If you find an error, write to <a href="mailto:info@medical-rank.com">info@medical-rank.com</a>. We fix confirmed errors and update the page's date.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
